contracts.error_cases:
null (key present) for:
- a folder root;
- a share or mapped network drive, or a SUBST letter over one;
- a figure that did not land within the bound;
- a stopped scan, Could not read, or Refused;
- an over-count (unseen < 0);
- the time from scan start until the panel is drawn.
sizeNotRead is null when ProbeFailures == 0. measured is [] when the volume is not NTFS, the $MFT read failed, or $MFT > unseen.

contracts.notes:
Pure and link-compiled into Core.Tests. Invariants pinned by unit tests:
- measured bytes + remainder bytes == unseen;
- the remainder text matches '(?i)cannot read' and never matches '(?i)(?<!not |never )\bmeasured\b';
- it contains 'container layer' if and only if includesStore;
- the measured text matches '(?i)\bmeasured\b';
- Folders carry no text and no size;
- no text outside ScreenLines contains a path separator.

key_decisions.rationale:
On a share, GetDiskFreeSpaceExW reports the server volume's figures (measured: Z:\ here reports 3.6 GB used), and the scan saw one folder of it. No wording makes that gap true, and the code already says a share adds no line (MainWindow.xaml.cs:689).

Asking the handle covers the alias classes a shape check cannot tell apart (#13):
- mapped letter: none;
- DFS letter: none;
- SUBST over a UNC path or mapped folder: none;
- SUBST over a local folder: line and panel, figure of the volume under it (existing m3);
- \\?\X:\: same as X:\;
- UNC root, volume mounted on a folder, junction-backed root: not drive roots, none, as today.
On the thread, a dead server can hold neither the scan nor its cancel (O-031).
